## Rotating Card – CSS + HTML

Below is a minimal, self‑contained example that shows a card which flips (rotates) around the Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy‑paste the code into an `.html` file and open it in a browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card</title>
<style>
/* ---------- 1️⃣  Container ---------- */
.card-wrapper {
  perspective: 1000px;          /* gives depth to the 3D effect */
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  margin: 50px auto;
}

/* ---------- 2️⃣  Card (the rotating element) ---------- */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  position: relative;
  transform-style: preserve-3d;   /* keep children in 3D space */
  transition: transform 0.8s ease; /* smooth rotation */
}

/* Hover triggers the flip */
.card-wrapper:hover .card {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
}

/* ---------- 3️⃣  Front & Back faces ---------- */
.card-face {
  position: absolute;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  backface-visibility: hidden;   /* hide the back side when facing away */
  border-radius: 10px;
  overflow: hidden;
  box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
}

.card-front {
  background: #fff;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  font-size: 1.5rem;
  color: #333;
}

.card-back {
  background: #4a90e2;
  color: #fff;
  transform: rotateY(180deg);     /* start rotated so it becomes visible on flip */
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  font-size: 1.2rem;
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-face card-front">
      Front Side
    </div>
    <div class="card-face card-back">
      Back Side
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens |
|------|--------------|
| **1** | `perspective` on the wrapper creates a 3‑D space. |
| **2** | `.card` is the element that will rotate. `transform-style: preserve-3d` keeps its children in 3‑D. |
| **3** | On hover, the card is rotated 180° around the Y‑axis. |
| **4** | Each face (`.card-front`, `.card-back`) is absolutely positioned and has `backface-visibility: hidden` so the hidden side disappears when turned away. |
| **5** | The back face is initially rotated 180° so that it becomes visible after the card flips. |

Feel free to replace the text, colors, or add images inside the faces. You can also change `rotateY` to `rotateX` for a vertical flip, or adjust the transition duration to suit your design.
